module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Division
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.KeyLemma.TameSymbolReciprocityWitness

/-!
# A nonzero summand of the reciprocity sum

The reciprocity relation Stacks 0EAW asserts that the sum

`∑_𝔮 ord_{A/𝔮}(∂_{A_𝔮}(a, b))`

over the height-one primes of a two-dimensional Noetherian ring vanishes. Every statement about
that sum is a statement about `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt`, and a vanishing-sum theorem about
an identically-zero summand carries no information. This file computes the summand at a prime
where it is **not** zero, so the reciprocity statements are about a function that genuinely takes
nonzero values.

The computation is the one Stacks 0EAN prescribes. If the first argument `a` avoids the prime
`𝔮` then it becomes a unit of `A_𝔮`, so `∂_{A_𝔮}(a, b) = ā^m` with
`m = length_{A_𝔮}(A_𝔮 / b A_𝔮)`, and therefore

`ord_{A/𝔮}(∂_{A_𝔮}(a, b)) = m · ord_{A/𝔮}(ā)`.

Both factors are orders of vanishing of elements of rings — `Stacks.Chow.ordInt` of the image of
a ring element — and `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_ord_mul_ord` evaluates the summand as
their product. This is the companion of
`Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_zero_of_isUnit_left`, which is the case where `a` is a unit of
`A` and the second factor is therefore zero; here `a` is a unit only of `A_𝔮`, and the second
factor can be anything.

At the witness ring `k[X₀, X₁]`, with the canonical tame symbols of
`Stacks.Chow.normalHeightOneSymbol`, both factors are `1` for `a = X₁`, `b = X₀` at the
height-one prime `(X₀)`: the localization `k[X₀, X₁]_{(X₀)}` is a discrete valuation ring in
which `X₀` generates the maximal ideal, and the class of `X₁` generates a maximal ideal of
`k[X₀, X₁] / (X₀)`. So the summand is `1`, and by skewness the summand of the same pair at the
height-one prime `(X₁)` is `-1`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX` — the height-one prime `(X_i)` of `k[X₀, X₁]`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.ordInt_algebraMap_eq_ord` — the order of vanishing of the image of a ring element
  is its `Ring.ord`, with no locality hypothesis.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_eq_one_of_isMaximal` — an element generating a maximal ideal has
  `Ring.ord` equal to `1`.
* `Stacks.Chow.heightOneOrd_eq_ord_quotient` — the order of vanishing along `A / 𝔮` of the
  residue of an element of `A` avoiding `𝔮`, as a `Ring.ord` in `A / 𝔮`.
* `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_ord_mul_ord` — the summand of Stacks 0EAW when the first
  argument avoids the prime, as a product of two orders of vanishing.
* `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_one`,
  `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_neg_one` — **the summand of Stacks 0EAW is
  `1` at one height-one prime of `k[X₀, X₁]` and `-1` at another**, for the pair `X₁`, `X₀`.
* `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_support_nonempty_mvPolynomial`,
  `Stacks.Chow.finite_and_nonempty_tameSymbolOrderAt_support_mvPolynomial`,
  `Stacks.Chow.not_forall_tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_zero_mvPolynomial` — the consequences: the set
  whose finiteness Stacks 0EAW asserts is finite and not empty, and the summand is not
  identically zero.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Chow.ordInt_algebraMap_eq_ord` is `StacksDraft.ordInt_algebraMap` with the hypothesis
`[IsLocalRing R]` removed; that hypothesis is not needed, and it cannot be met here, because
`A / 𝔮` is not local for a height-one prime of a two-dimensional ring; the proof of
`StacksDraft.ordInt_algebraMap` goes through verbatim without it. The
proof here goes through `Ring.ordMonoidWithZeroHom_eq_coe` instead.

The maximality of the ideal generated by the class of `X_j` in `k[X₀, X₁] / (X_i)` is obtained
from the maximality of `(X₀, X₁)` in `k[X₀, X₁]` — the kernel of evaluation at the origin,
`Stacks.Chow.ker_eval_zero_mvPolynomial` — through `DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup`. No
isomorphism `k[X₀, X₁] / (X₀) ≅ k[X₁]` is needed, and none exists in Mathlib at this pin.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EAW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EAW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EAN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EAN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

section OrderOfVanishing

/-- **The order of vanishing of the image of a ring element is its `Ring.ord`.** This is
`StacksDraft.ordInt_algebraMap` without the hypothesis that `R` is local, which is not needed:
the order of vanishing is read off `Ring.ordMonoidWithZeroHom`, whose value on a nonzerodivisor
is the (finite) `Ring.ord`. The locality hypothesis cannot be met for the quotient of a
two-dimensional ring by a height-one prime, which is where this is used. -/
theorem ordInt_algebraMap_eq_ord (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 R] {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    (r : R) (hr : r ≠ 0) (hr' : algebraMap R K r ≠ 0) :
    ordInt R (algebraMap R K r) hr' = ((Ring.ord R r).toNat : ℤ) := by
  have hr0 : r ∈ nonZeroDivisors R := mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hr
  have hn : Ring.ord R r = ((Ring.ord R r).toNat : ℕ∞) :=
    (ENat.natCast_toNat (Ring.ord_ne_top hr0)).symm
  have hfrac : Ring.ordFrac R (K := K) (algebraMap R K r) =
      ((Multiplicative.ofAdd (((Ring.ord R r).toNat : ℤ)) : Multiplicative ℤ) :
        WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) := by
    rw [Ring.ordFrac_eq_ord R hr, Ring.ordMonoidWithZeroHom_eq_coe R hr0 hn]
  unfold ordInt
  have h : WithZero.unzero (x := Ring.ordFrac R (K := K) (algebraMap R K r))
      ((hr'.isUnit.map (Ring.ordFrac R)).ne_zero) =
      (Multiplicative.ofAdd (((Ring.ord R r).toNat : ℤ)) : Multiplicative ℤ) := by
    rw [← WithZero.coe_inj, WithZero.coe_unzero, hfrac]
  rw [h]
  simp

/-- **An element generating a maximal ideal has order of vanishing one**, because the quotient by
a maximal ideal is a field, hence a simple module. This is Mathlib's `Ring.ord_of_irreducible`
with the principal-ideal-ring hypothesis replaced by the maximality it is used to produce. -/
theorem ord_eq_one_of_isMaximal {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {x : R}
    (h : (Ideal.span {x}).IsMaximal) : Ring.ord R x = 1 := by
  rw [Ring.ord, Module.length_eq_one_iff,
    isSimpleModule_iff_isSimpleModule_of_algebraMap_surjective (S := R ⧸ Ideal.span {x})
      Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective]
  let _ := Ideal.Quotient.field (Ideal.span {x})
  exact instIsSimpleModule _

/-- **In the localization at a principal prime, the image of the generator generates the maximal
ideal**, hence a maximal ideal. -/
theorem isMaximal_span_algebraMap_atPrime {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {x : A}
    [(Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A).IsPrime] :
    (Ideal.span {algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.span {x})) x}).IsMaximal := by
  have h : Ideal.span {algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.span {x})) x} =
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime (Ideal.span {x})) := by
    rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  exact h ▸ maximalIdeal.isMaximal _

end OrderOfVanishing

section Summand

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]

/-- **The order of vanishing along a height-one prime of the residue of an element avoiding
it.** For `x : A` outside `𝔮` the class of `x` in `A / 𝔮` is nonzero, and the order of vanishing
of its residue is the `Ring.ord` of that class. This is the nonzero counterpart of
`Stacks.Chow.heightOneOrd_eq_zero_of_isUnit`, which is the case where `x` is a unit of `A` and
the `Ring.ord` is therefore zero. -/
theorem heightOneOrd_eq_ord_quotient (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (p : HeightOnePrime A)
    (w : (ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal))ˣ) {x : A}
    (hx : x ∉ p.1.asIdeal)
    (hw : (w : ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)) =
      residue (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)
        (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal) x)) :
    heightOneOrd hdim p w =
      ((Ring.ord (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal) (Ideal.Quotient.mk p.1.asIdeal x)).toNat : ℤ) := by
  let _ : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal) :=
    krullDimLE_quotient_of_height_eq_one hdim p.1.asIdeal p.2
  have hval : (w : ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)) =
      algebraMap (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal) (ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal))
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk p.1.asIdeal x) := by
    rw [hw, residue_algebraMap_eq]
  have hmkne : Ideal.Quotient.mk p.1.asIdeal x ≠ 0 := mt Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp hx
  have hne : algebraMap (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal)
      (ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal))
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk p.1.asIdeal x) ≠ 0 := hval ▸ w.ne_zero
  change ordInt (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal)
    (w : ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)) w.ne_zero = _
  rw [ordInt_val_congr (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal) hval w.ne_zero hne,
    ordInt_algebraMap_eq_ord _ _ hmkne hne]

/-- **The summand of Stacks 0EAW when the first argument avoids the prime.** By Stacks 0EAN the
symbol is then the residue of the first argument raised to `length_{A_𝔮}(A_𝔮 / b A_𝔮)`, so the
summand is that length times the order of vanishing of the class of the first argument in
`A / 𝔮`:

`ord_{A/𝔮}(∂_{A_𝔮}(a, b)) = length_{A_𝔮}(A_𝔮 / b A_𝔮) · ord_{A/𝔮}(ā)`.

`Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_zero_of_isUnit_left` is the special case where `a` is a unit of
`A`, in which the second factor vanishes; in general it need not. -/
theorem tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_ord_mul_ord (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (p : HeightOnePrime A)
    (symb : RegularTameSymbol (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)) (a b : nonZeroDivisors A)
    (ha : (a : A) ∉ p.1.asIdeal) :
    tameSymbolOrderAt hdim p symb a b =
      (Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)
          (toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor p.1.asIdeal b :
            Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)).toNat *
        ((Ring.ord (A ⧸ p.1.asIdeal) (Ideal.Quotient.mk p.1.asIdeal (a : A))).toNat : ℤ) := by
  have hau : IsUnit ((toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor p.1.asIdeal a :
      Localization.AtPrime p.1.asIdeal)) :=
    isUnit_toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor p.1.asIdeal a ha
  rw [show tameSymbolOrderAt hdim p symb a b =
      heightOneOrd hdim p (symb (toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor p.1.asIdeal a)
        (toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor p.1.asIdeal b)) from rfl,
    symb.unit_left _ _ hau.unit hau.unit_spec.symm, heightOneOrd_pow,
    heightOneOrd_eq_ord_quotient hdim p _ ha (by simp [toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor])]

end Summand

section Witness

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- The ideal generated by a variable of `k[X₀, X₁]` is prime: a variable is a prime element. -/
theorem isPrime_span_mvPolynomialX (i : Fin 2) :
    (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).IsPrime :=
  (Ideal.span_singleton_prime (MvPolynomial.X_ne_zero i)).mpr MvPolynomial.X_prime

/-- The ideal generated by a variable of `k[X₀, X₁]` has height one: it is generated by a
nonzerodivisor which is not a unit. -/
theorem height_span_mvPolynomialX (i : Fin 2) :
    (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).height = 1 :=
  Ideal.height_span_singleton_eq_one_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors
    (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero (MvPolynomial.X_ne_zero i))
    (not_isUnit_mvPolynomial_X k i)

/-- The height-one prime `(X_i)` of `k[X₀, X₁]`. -/
noncomputable def mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX (i : Fin 2) :
    HeightOnePrime (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) :=
  ⟨⟨Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i}, isPrime_span_mvPolynomialX k i⟩,
    height_span_mvPolynomialX k i⟩

/-- The ideal underlying the height-one prime `(X_i)` of `k[X₀, X₁]` is `(X_i)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem asIdeal_mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX (i : Fin 2) :
    (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal = Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} := rfl

/-- A variable of `k[X₀, X₁]` does not lie in the ideal generated by the other one: evaluating at
the point where the first is `0` and the second is `1` would make `1 = 0`. -/
theorem notMem_span_mvPolynomialX {i j : Fin 2} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    (MvPolynomial.X j : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) ∉
      (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal := by
  intro h
  rw [asIdeal_mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at h
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h
  have he := congrArg
    (MvPolynomial.eval (fun l : Fin 2 => if l = i then (0 : k) else 1)) hc
  simp [hij.symm] at he

/-- The difference of a polynomial and its constant term lies in the ideal generated by the
variables: every other monomial is divisible by one of them. -/
theorem sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_span_mvPolynomialX (f : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) :
    f - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff f) ∈
      (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X 0, MvPolynomial.X 1} :
        Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)) := by
  refine MvPolynomial.induction_on
    (motive := fun g => g - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff g) ∈
      (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X 0, MvPolynomial.X 1} :
        Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))) f ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro a
    simp
  · intro p q hp hq
    have hpq : p + q - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff (p + q)) =
        (p - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff p)) +
          (q - MvPolynomial.C (MvPolynomial.constantCoeff q)) := by
      simp only [map_add]
      ring
    rw [hpq]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ hp hq
  · intro p n _
    have hc : MvPolynomial.constantCoeff (p * MvPolynomial.X n) = 0 := by simp
    rw [hc, map_zero, sub_zero]
    refine Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ?_
    fin_cases n <;> exact Ideal.subset_span (by simp)

/-- **The ideal generated by the variables of `k[X₀, X₁]` is the kernel of evaluation at the
origin.** -/
theorem ker_eval_zero_mvPolynomial :
    RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.eval (fun _ : Fin 2 => (0 : k))) =
      (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X 0, MvPolynomial.X 1} :
        Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · intro f hf
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, MvPolynomial.eval_zero'] at hf
    have h := sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_span_mvPolynomialX k f
    rwa [hf, map_zero, sub_zero] at h
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro y (rfl | rfl) <;> exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (by rw [MvPolynomial.eval_X])

/-- **The ideal generated by two distinct variables of `k[X₀, X₁]` is maximal**, being the kernel
of a surjection onto the field `k`. -/
theorem isMaximal_span_pair_mvPolynomialX {i j : Fin 2} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i, MvPolynomial.X j} :
      Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).IsMaximal := by
  have h01 : (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X 0, MvPolynomial.X 1} :
      Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).IsMaximal := by
    rw [← ker_eval_zero_mvPolynomial]
    exact RingHom.ker_isMaximal_of_surjective _ fun a => ⟨MvPolynomial.C a, by simp⟩
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp_all [Set.pair_comm]

/-- **The class of a variable generates a maximal ideal of the quotient by another variable.**
This is the maximality of the ideal generated by the two variables, transported along
`DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup`. -/
theorem isMaximal_span_quotientMk_mvPolynomialX {i j : Fin 2} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    (Ideal.span {(Ideal.Quotient.mk
      (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))
      (MvPolynomial.X j))}).IsMaximal := by
  have hmap : (Ideal.span {(Ideal.Quotient.mk
      (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))
      (MvPolynomial.X j))}) =
      Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i}))
        (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X j}) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.maximal_ideal_iff_isField_quotient, hmap]
  refine (DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup
    (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))
    (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X j})).toMulEquiv.isField ?_
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.maximal_ideal_iff_isField_quotient,
    show (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} ⊔ Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X j} :
        Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)) =
      Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i, MvPolynomial.X j} from (Ideal.span_insert _ _).symm]
  exact isMaximal_span_pair_mvPolynomialX k hij

/-- **A NONZERO SUMMAND OF THE RECIPROCITY SUM OF STACKS 0EAW.** At the height-one prime `(X_i)`
of `k[X₀, X₁]`, with the canonical tame symbol of `Stacks.Chow.normalHeightOneSymbol`, the
summand of Stacks 0EAW at the pair `X_j`, `X_i` with `j ≠ i` is `1`:

`ord_{A/(X_i)}(∂_{A_{(X_i)}}(X_j, X_i)) = 1`.

Both factors of `Stacks.Chow.tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_ord_mul_ord` are `1`: in the discrete
valuation ring `k[X₀, X₁]_{(X_i)}` the image of `X_i` generates the maximal ideal, and the class
of `X_j` generates a maximal ideal of `k[X₀, X₁] / (X_i)`. -/
theorem tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_one {i j : Fin 2} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k)
        (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i)
        (normalHeightOneSymbol (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i))
        (mvPolynomialX k j) (mvPolynomialX k i) = 1 := by
  have _i : (Ideal.span {MvPolynomial.X i} : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)).IsPrime :=
    isPrime_span_mvPolynomialX k i
  have hlocal : Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal)
      ((toLocalizationNonZeroDivisor (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal
        (mvPolynomialX k i) :
          Localization.AtPrime (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal)) = 1 := by
    refine ord_eq_one_of_isMaximal ?_
    exact isMaximal_span_algebraMap_atPrime
      (A := MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) (x := MvPolynomial.X i)
  have hquot : Ring.ord
      (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal)
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k i).1.asIdeal
        ((mvPolynomialX k j : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))) = 1 :=
    ord_eq_one_of_isMaximal (isMaximal_span_quotientMk_mvPolynomialX k hij)
  rw [tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_ord_mul_ord _ _ _ _ _ (notMem_span_mvPolynomialX k hij),
    hlocal, hquot]
  rfl

/-- **The summand of Stacks 0EAW at the other height-one prime is `-1`**, by skewness: the two
summands of the pair `X_j`, `X_i` at the prime `(X_j)` are opposite, and the one with the
arguments in the other order is `1`. So the summand takes both signs, and the vanishing of the
reciprocity sum is not the vanishing of its terms. -/
theorem tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_neg_one {i j : Fin 2} (hij : i ≠ j) :
    tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k)
        (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k j)
        (normalHeightOneSymbol (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k j))
        (mvPolynomialX k j) (mvPolynomialX k i) = -1 := by
  have h := tameSymbolOrderAt_add_swap (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k)
    (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k j)
    (normalHeightOneSymbol (mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k j))
    (mvPolynomialX k j) (mvPolynomialX k i)
  rw [tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_one k hij.symm] at h
  linarith

/-- **The set whose finiteness Stacks 0EAW asserts is not empty.** Together with
`Stacks.Chow.finite_tameSymbolOrderAt_support_mvPolynomial` this says that the finiteness
assertion of Stacks 0EAW is about a nonempty finite set of height-one primes. -/
theorem tameSymbolOrderAt_support_nonempty_mvPolynomial :
    {p : HeightOnePrime (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) |
      tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k) p (normalHeightOneSymbol p)
        (mvPolynomialX k 1) (mvPolynomialX k 0) ≠ 0}.Nonempty :=
  ⟨mvPolynomialHeightOnePrimeX k 0, fun h0 =>
    one_ne_zero
      ((tameSymbolOrderAt_mvPolynomialX_eq_one k (i := 0) (j := 1)
        (by decide)).symm.trans h0)⟩

/-- **The index set of the sum of Stacks 0EAW is finite and not empty.** One set expression,
carrying both the finiteness `Stacks.Chow.finite_tameSymbolOrderAt_support_mvPolynomial` that
Stacks 0EAW asserts and the nonemptiness just proved: the exhibited nonzero summand lies in the
very set whose finiteness is the content of the first half of Stacks 0EAW. -/
theorem finite_and_nonempty_tameSymbolOrderAt_support_mvPolynomial :
    {p : HeightOnePrime (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) |
        tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k) p (normalHeightOneSymbol p)
          (mvPolynomialX k 1) (mvPolynomialX k 0) ≠ 0}.Finite ∧
      {p : HeightOnePrime (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k) |
        tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k) p (normalHeightOneSymbol p)
          (mvPolynomialX k 1) (mvPolynomialX k 0) ≠ 0}.Nonempty :=
  ⟨finite_tameSymbolOrderAt_support_mvPolynomial k _ _,
    tameSymbolOrderAt_support_nonempty_mvPolynomial k⟩

/-- **The summand of Stacks 0EAW is not identically zero.** So the vanishing-sum statements of
Stacks 0EAW are not statements about the zero function, and the hypotheses under which the
summand is proved to vanish are not vacuous. -/
theorem not_forall_tameSymbolOrderAt_eq_zero_mvPolynomial :
    ¬ ∀ (p : HeightOnePrime (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k))
        (a b : nonZeroDivisors (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)),
      tameSymbolOrderAt (MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_fin_two k) p (normalHeightOneSymbol p)
        a b = 0 := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := tameSymbolOrderAt_support_nonempty_mvPolynomial k
  exact hp (h p _ _)

end Witness

end Stacks.Chow

